   ],
   "html": "<p>The concept brings together the city’s most iconic nightlife brands and record labels, including <strong>Brownies &amp; Lemonade</strong>, <strong>Emo Nite</strong>, <strong>Ninja Tune</strong>, <strong>Mad Decent</strong> and more, all under one roof as a celebration of the community and a thank you to the city for all it's given us.</p>\n<p>The epic event took place the week before Christmas at <strong>Jewel’s Catch One</strong> (except 2019, at <strong>The Belasco</strong>) with 100% of all proceeds raised going to <strong>Downtown Women’s Center,</strong> <strong>My Friends Place</strong>, and others.</p>"
  }
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "The Origin Story",
   "pieces": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "html": "<p>In 2016, <strong>IHC</strong> launched an annual charity event and auction that brought together LA’s most impactful music curators, influencers, and businesses. Inspired by our roots as promoters, the core of the idea came from a desire for community. As the homeless crisis in LA evolved, demanding more action and awareness, we partnered with <strong>Brownies &amp; Lemonade</strong>, <strong>Shrek Rave</strong>, <strong>Club 90s</strong>, <strong>Hack The Planet</strong>, <strong>Heav3n</strong>, and more to bring community and raise money for our city. </p>"
    },
